!!! =============================================================================
!!! sdkinstaller — Installer configuration and state types
!!! =============================================================================
!!!
!!! The installer configuration model. Types for workloads, components,
!!! install state, and environment variables. These are the shared records
!!! used across the installer modules.
!!!
!!! All persistence uses nil.std.nildata for versioned, validated storage.
!!! =============================================================================

book sdkinstaller.config

read nil.std.core.option
read nil.std.core.result
read nil.std.nildata


!!! --- ComponentKind: what kind of thing a component represents.
!!!
!!! A component can be a set of framework files (the default), a system
!!! package, an environment hook, or a generated entry point.

public ComponentKind begin choice
    when FrameworkFiles
    when SystemPackage
    when EnvHook
    when GeneratedTemplate
end choice


!!! --- A single component that the installer knows how to lay down.
!!!
!!! Components are the atomic unit of installation. A workload selects a
!!! set of components; the installer resolves dependencies transitively.
!!!
!!! `id` is the stable identifier used in CLI flags and saved manifests.
!!! `name` and `description` are for display.
!!! `kind` controls how the component is installed.
!!! `sizeBytes` is an estimate for progress display.
!!! `dependencies` lists component IDs that must also be installed.
!!! `sourcePath` is the SDK-relative directory or glob for framework files.
!!! `envVar` / `envValue` are set when kind is EnvHook.
!!! `templatePath` is the SDK-relative path to a template file when kind is
!!! GeneratedTemplate.

public Component begin record
    field id as text
    field name as text
    field description as text
    field kind as ComponentKind
    field sizeBytes as number
    field dependencies as array of text
    field sourcePath as text
    field envVar as text
    field envValue as text
    field templatePath as text
end record


!!! --- A workload is a named, curated set of components, like VS installer
!!! workloads. The "core" workload is always available.

public Workload begin record
    field id as text
    field name as text
    field description as text
    field componentIds as array of text
end record


!!! --- InstallLocation: where the SDK components are laid down.
!!!
!!! `path` is the absolute destination directory. `isCustom` is true when
!!! the user chose a non-default location.

public InstallLocation begin record
    field path as text
    field isCustom as boolean
end record


!!! --- Selection: which workloads and components are selected for install.
!!!
!!! `workloadIds` is the set of workloads the user selected.
!!! `componentExclusions` are component IDs the user explicitly deselected
!!! (e.g. via --without). The installer computes the final component set
!!! from the workload closure minus exclusions.

public Selection begin record
    field workloadIds as array of text
    field componentExclusions as array of text
end record


!!! --- InstallState: the on-disk record of what was installed.
!!!
!!! Written as `sdkinstaller-state.nildata` in the install location.
!!! `installedComponentIds` records exactly what was laid down.
!!! `sdkPath` is the absolute install root.
!!! `sdkVersion` is the NIL SDK version at install time.
!!! `installedAt` is an ISO-8601 timestamp.

public InstallState begin record
    field installedComponentIds as array of text
    field sdkPath as text
    field sdkVersion as text
    field installedAt as text
end record


!!! --- EnvEntry: a single environment variable to set.
!!!
!!! `name` is the variable name (e.g. "NIL_SDK_PATH").
!!! `value` is the literal value to set.
!!! `prependPath` is an optional path to prepend to the variable when it is
!!! PATH-like (e.g. "bin" relative to the SDK root).

public EnvEntry begin record
    field name as text
    field value as text
    field prependPath as text
end record


!!! --- FilePlanEntry: a single file to copy during installation.
!!!
!!! Source is relative to the SDK root; destination is relative to the
!!! install location. The installer de-duplicates by destination path.

public FilePlanEntry begin record
    field sourceRel as text
    field destRel as text
end record


!!! --- FilePlan: the resolved plan of what to copy.
!!!
!!! `entries` is the de-duplicated list of files to install.
!!! `totalBytes` is the estimated sum of file sizes.

public FilePlan begin record
    field entries as array of FilePlanEntry
    field totalBytes as number
end record


!!! --- InstallResult: what happened after running the installer.
!!!
!!! `success` is true if everything installed without error.
!!! `installedComponents` is the list of component IDs that were installed.
!!! `envEntries` is the environment configuration that was written.
!!! `error` is set if installation failed.

public InstallResult begin record
    field success as boolean
    field installedComponents as array of text
    field envEntries as array of EnvEntry
    field error as Option of text
end record


!!! --- ResolveResult: the outcome of resolving a selection into components.
!!!
!!! `components` is the full transitive closure of components to install.
!!! `missingDependencies` lists component IDs that were referenced but not
!!! available in the registry.

public ResolveResult begin record
    field components as array of Component
    field missingDependencies as array of text
end record
